ple  will say David you've got to talk about  the results  the poll about medicare-for-all the same  poll shows medicare-for-all as described  in the poll is not that popular there's  a question in this Fox News poll about  replacing the private health insurance  system that we have with a  government-run program it has only 41  percent support now we know from  experience that the wording on that  question really influences what people  say so on the one hand you can almost  guarantee low support for Medicare for  all type system if you say something  like do you support a government  takeover of health care that wording  will get a low level of support on the  other hand you can get a very high level  of support for Medicare for all if you  phrase it as should the government  provide a basic level of care to  everyone regardless of ability to pay  even though that's not exactly what  Medicare for all is but the point is the  wording of these health care questions  really influenced the support now that  being said I want to tell everyone Fox  News polls are considered pretty solid  they are rated a by a number of  different organizations that rate  pollsters including 538 this says  nothing about Fox News TV channel it  says nothing about the content of Fox  News Radio their polling is considered  relatively good polling so I do think we  need to accept when they say 68% favor  of wealth tax it's probably close to  that when they say only 41% support  replacing private insurance with a  government-run plant run plan it's  probably close to that that doesn't mean  that the question is asked in the way  that most clearly explains what it is  that's being proposed but that's part of  the problem part of the problem is the  messaging and that people don't  understand what it is that's being  proposed it also by the way doesn't mean  that a government-run program is bad all  the poll tells us is that there's a long  way to go in garnering more public  support and much 